@startuml module

namespace Module <<unit>> {
    class "Worker"
    class ModuleClient
    Worker ..> ModuleClient
}

' This case tests supported declarations of the same Worker in multiple unit
' groups; it is not a recommendation to assign one class to multiple units.
' Prefer declaring Worker and the relevant Clients in an overview and drawing
' these dependencies there. Keep Worker's member definition in one detail file.
' Module/Other diagrams need no Worker declaration if they no longer draw
' relationships sourced from Worker; otherwise the source must be declared locally.
' For the recommended organization, see the sibling test case:
' plantuml/parser/integration_test/class_diagram/grouping_containers_overview_dependencies

@enduml
